 "finding": "Under the standard ratio margin every conclusion holds and two of them strengthen. morisien-embed-v1.5 beats untrained LaBSE by 0.0411 error rate against 0.0321 under cosine, and morisien-embed falls further behind it, 0.0161 against 0.0071. Margin scoring raises the error rate for the three stronger models and lowers it for multilingual-e5-base, the only model whose gold is often outside the top-4 by cosine.",
 "caveats": [
  "One run per model. The encoders are deterministic here, but this has not been repeated.",
  "The margin reranks only the k=4 nearest cosine neighbours, so it can demote a gold that cosine ranked first as well as promote one it ranked second to fourth. Both directions occur.",
  "Per-query vectors exist for LaBSE and v1.5 only. A paired test against morisien-embed or multilingual-e5-base needs a re-run with --per-query."
 ],
